WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.630
Do not assign classmates' photos.

2
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.330
The drawn set is the seminar, and the

3
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.130
mark is a sentence: who was missed.

4
00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.410
In the seminar: one average, one

5
00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.510
line, and a miss you make them

6
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.130
write before any real system.

7
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.580
The score is how close a picture is to

8
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.520
the average of the training faces.

9
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.280
The line is the same for every picture.

10
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.690
The wide face falls below the line.

11
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.450
The box stays below it too,

12
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.230
and that part is correct.

13
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.620
A test on only the training

14
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.240
shape hides the miss.

15
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.980
These are drawings, not

16
00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:42.880
anyone's photograph.

17
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.670
Close-set eyes sit in the average.

18
00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.890
Spread them out and the score drops,

19
00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.270
even though it is still a face.

20
00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:54.110
Quick check!

21
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.130
The detector trained on close-set eyes.

22
00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.160
A wider drawn face scores where?

23
00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.320
Below the line.

24
00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.260
Same idea, wider spacing, and

25
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.660
the match falls short.

26
00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.310
Students write the miss in one sentence

27
00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:14.450
before you discuss a real detector.

28
00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.670
If someone opens a camera

29
00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.110
roll, stop the exercise.

30
00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:20.290
Your turn.

31
00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.210
Is a high score on the training shape

32
00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:26.070
enough to trust a detector on new people?

33
00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:28.080
Remember this.

34
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:29.980
Report who was missed.

35
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.870
Do not test a face detector on

36
00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.310
real photographs of people.

37
00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:36.910
Try it in your next lecture.

38
00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.610
Add one line to the lab sheet:

39
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.510
photographs of people are out of scope.
